            <ArticleTitle>Erythroplasia of Queyrat treated with topical 5-fluorouracil.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>42-44</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0365-05962016001100042</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1590/abd1806-4841.20164595</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a 33-year-old male patient diagnosed with erythroplasia of Queyrat. The patient had an erythematous and eroded lesion affecting more than 50% of the glans associated with bleeding and local pain. Despite previous indication of penectomy, he was successfully treated with topical 5-fluorouracil.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
